NNAAMMEE
     hhttttppdd — HTTP daemon

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     hhttttppdd [--ddnnvv] [--DD _m_a_c_r_o=_v_a_l_u_e] [--ff _f_i_l_e]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The hhttttppdd daemon is an HTTP server with FastCGI and TLS support.

     The FastCGI implementation has optional socket support.  hhttttppdd can log to
     syslog(3) or per-server files with several standard formats.

     hhttttppdd rereads its configuration file when it receives SIGHUP and reopens
     log files when it receives SIGUSR1.

     The options are as follows:

     --DD _m_a_c_r_o=_v_a_l_u_e  Set a _m_a_c_r_o to a _v_a_l_u_e.  Macros can be referenced in the
                     configuration files.

     --dd              Debug mode.  Create one server and don't detach or become
                     a daemon.  This allows for easy monitoring of hhttttppdd.

     --ff _f_i_l_e         Specifies the configuration file.  The default is
                     _/_e_t_c_/_h_t_t_p_d_._c_o_n_f.

     --nn              Check that the configuration is valid, but don't start
                     any servers.

     --vv              Verbose mode.  Multiple --vv options increase the ver‐
                     bosity.

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/httpd.conf              Default configuration file.
     /etc/ssl/private/server.key  Default SSL/TLS server key.
     /etc/ssl/server.crt          Default SSL/TLS server certificate.
     /var/www/logs/access.log     Default access log file.
     /var/www/logs/error.log      Default error log file.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     acme-client(1), httpd.conf(5), slowcgi(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The hhttttppdd program first appeared in OpenBSD 5.6.  hhttttppdd is based on
     relayd(8).

